{
  "sentinel": "COAI-FIXTURE-SENTINEL",
  "notes": "The ONE list of structural fields in a caller-transcript fixture, read by scripts/cut-transcript-fixtures.mjs and by the C# guard. Every string leaf is the sentinel unless its dotted path is listed here AND its value satisfies the shape; the sentinel itself is valid at ANY string position (a value that failed its shape was replaced by it). Booleans and nulls are kept; a number is kept only at a path whose shape is int, and there it is a non-negative integer, redrawn as the RANK of its value among the fixture's values at that path (0 stays 0; spawnDepth is structural and kept); every other number, a fraction and a negative included, is 0. An instant (iso-utc) is redrawn on a synthetic clock: 2000-01-01T00:00:00Z plus one second per rank of the fixture's distinct real instants. Paths are dotted, [] marks an array element. An object key survives only if it is a segment of some path below (the closed key set); every other key is k<n>, numbered per object, and nothing under a renamed key is allowlisted. A shape is the regex in shapes (anchored with ^ and $; .NET callers use \\z for the end anchor), enum:<a|b|..>, int, bool, a vocabulary (the value is in its builtin list, or, where the vocabulary has a rewritten pattern, matches it: mcp tool names are mcp__s<n>__t<n>, a non-builtin agent type is custom-<n>; the model vocabularies are EXACT lists, anything else is the sentinel), or fixture-path: a fixture root (compared with the separators folded) followed by segments that each match ^p[0-9]+([.][a-z0-9]{1,5})?$. Widening this file is a privacy decision: ACallerTranscriptFixtureCarriesNoTextTests pins its hash, and the reviewer who changes it updates that hash deliberately.",
  "shapes": {
    "uuid": "^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$",
    "hexid": "^[0-9a-f]{8,64}$",
    "msgid": "^msg_[0-9A-Za-z]{8,64}$",
    "toolid": "^toolu_[0-9A-Za-z_]{8,80}$",
    "iso-utc": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}([.][0-9]{1,9})?Z$",
    "version": "^[0-9]{1,4}[.][0-9]{1,4}[.][0-9]{1,4}$"
  },
